WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.945
It is almost Christmas.

2
00:00:01.946 --> 00:00:07.022
Today the Smith family is going to get their Christmas tree.

3
00:00:07.023 --> 00:00:08.774
"Come on, Jay and Sarah.

4
00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.326
Let’s get going," says Dad.

5
00:00:11.327 --> 00:00:14.506
"Where are we going, Dad?" asks Jay.

6
00:00:14.507 --> 00:00:17.655
"We’re going to the Christmas tree farm."

7
00:00:17.656 --> 00:00:19.705
Jay and Sarah are excited.

8
00:00:19.706 --> 00:00:22.514
"All right!" they cheer.

9
00:00:22.515 --> 00:00:28.678
When the Smith family arrives at the tree farm, they see thousands of Christmas trees.

10
00:00:28.679 --> 00:00:30.728
"Look at all the trees.

11
00:00:30.729 --> 00:00:34.625
They are planted in straight rows," says Sarah.

12
00:00:34.626 --> 00:00:38.439
"They have many kinds of Christmas trees," Dad says.

13
00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:42.059
"Yes," says Mom, "those are white pines.

14
00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.929
And these are spruce trees."

15
00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:47.160
Picking a tree is not easy.

16
00:00:47.161 --> 00:00:49.214
Some trees are too small.

17
00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.933
Some trees are too big.

18
00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:54.104
Some trees are not straight.

19
00:00:54.105 --> 00:00:57.801
"How about this tree?" says Jay, pointing.

20
00:00:57.802 --> 00:01:00.932
"It’s too thin, Jay," Dad says.

21
00:01:00.933 --> 00:01:03.634
"What about that tree?" suggests Sarah.

22
00:01:03.635 --> 00:01:08.099
Mom disagrees. "It’s too twisty, Sarah."

23
00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.781
Then Mom finds a tall, straight tree.

24
00:01:10.782 --> 00:01:12.416
"I like that tree.

25
00:01:12.417 --> 00:01:15.609
It is a perfect Christmas tree."

26
00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:19.071
"Wow! I like it too," says Jay.

27
00:01:19.072 --> 00:01:21.690
"It’s beautiful," says Sarah.

28
00:01:21.691 --> 00:01:24.182
Dad agrees. "Let’s cut it down."

29
00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:31.031
With a chain saw, he cuts through the trunk of the tree. "Timber!"

30
00:01:31.032 --> 00:01:36.172
"Stay back, Jay. It’s going to fall," warns Mom.

31
00:01:36.173 --> 00:01:41.988
Mom and Dad go to pay for the tree, and Sarah and Jay enjoy a hot cup of apple cider.

32
00:01:41.989 --> 00:01:44.734
The tree farm makes delicious hot apple cider.

33
00:01:44.735 --> 00:01:46.658
Soon, it is time to go.

34
00:01:46.659 --> 00:01:47.846
"Thank you very much.

35
00:01:47.847 --> 00:01:51.095
Enjoy your tree," says the man at the tree farm.

36
00:01:51.096 --> 00:01:54.460
"Merry Christmas," the Smiths say.

37
00:01:54.461 --> 00:01:59.198
In the parking lot, they tie their new Christmas tree to the roof of the car.

38
00:01:59.199 --> 00:02:00.938
Then they drive home.

39
00:02:00.939 --> 00:02:03.278
Cutting down the tree is only half the fun.

40
00:02:03.279 --> 00:02:06.970
When they get home, it is time to decorate it.

41
00:02:06.971 --> 00:02:09.732
"Brush the snow off the tree," says Mom.

42
00:02:09.733 --> 00:02:12.843
"I’ll get the Christmas tree stand," says Dad.

43
00:02:12.844 --> 00:02:15.627
Dad puts the tree into the stand.

44
00:02:15.628 --> 00:02:18.767
Without the stand, the tree cannot stand up.

45
00:02:18.768 --> 00:02:21.587
"Now we can decorate the tree."

46
00:02:21.588 --> 00:02:25.171
"First we must put the lights on," says Mom.

47
00:02:25.172 --> 00:02:28.101
Sarah makes sure that every lightbulb works.

48
00:02:28.102 --> 00:02:30.440
Dad and Jay put the lights on the tree.

49
00:02:30.441 --> 00:02:32.132
"Look at this one.

50
00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:34.738
It’s pretty," says Sarah.

51
00:02:34.739 --> 00:02:38.605
"The tin soldiers are my favorite," says Jay.

52
00:02:38.606 --> 00:02:45.101
"Now, Jay and Sarah," says Mom, "you can put some tinsel on the tree."

53
00:02:45.102 --> 00:02:48.063
When they are done, Sarah is pleased.

54
00:02:48.064 --> 00:02:51.282
"Wow, it looks beautiful."

55
00:02:51.283 --> 00:02:52.913
The tree is almost finished.

56
00:02:52.914 --> 00:02:55.926
It looks great, but there is one thing missing.

57
00:02:55.927 --> 00:02:58.891
"The star!" says Mom.

58
00:02:58.892 --> 00:03:02.611
No Christmas tree is complete without a star on top.

59
00:03:02.612 --> 00:03:07.311
Dad lifts Jay up so that he can place the star on the top of the tree.

60
00:03:07.312 --> 00:03:09.397
"Perfect!" says Mom.

61
00:03:09.398 --> 00:03:14.077
"This is the greatest Christmas tree ever," says Sarah.

62
00:03:14.078 --> 00:03:21.966
And everyone agrees!

